# ============================================================================
# Musea Curator Tips — environment reference
# ============================================================================
#
# This file documents every variable the project needs and WHERE each one lives.
# It is committed; it must never contain a real value.
#
# There are two distinct places variables live, and mixing them up is a common
# time sink:
#
#   [CONVEX]  Set in the Convex dashboard -> Settings -> Environment Variables,
#             or via `npx convex env set NAME value`. These are server-side only
#             and are the ONLY place secrets may exist.
#
#   [WEB]     Set in apps/web/.env.local (and in Vercel project settings).
#             Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is embedded in the browser bundle
#             and is therefore PUBLIC. Never put a secret behind that prefix.
#
# Every [CONVEX] Stellar variable is read and validated in
# packages/backend/convex/stellar/config.ts, which fails at first use with a
# sentence you can act on rather than an opaque error later.
#
# The values this deployment uses (for the public ones) are listed in
# docs/evidence.md, section 3.2.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [CONVEX] Stellar network
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
STELLAR_NETWORK=testnet
HORIZON_URL=https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org
RPC_URL=https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org
# Exact string, spaces and semicolon included. A mismatch with STELLAR_NETWORK
# makes every transaction fail with an invalid signature — config.ts checks for
# exactly this pairing because it is the mistake that costs the most time.
NETWORK_PASSPHRASE=Test SDF Network ; September 2015
FRIENDBOT_URL=https://friendbot.stellar.org

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [CONVEX] Assets and contracts — produced by scripts/setup-testnet.sh
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# XLM is the network's native asset: no issuer, no asset code, no trustline for
# anyone. The SAC address is DERIVED from the network passphrase rather than
# chosen, so a testnet value is wrong on pubnet and vice versa.
XLM_SAC_ID=                  # C... native XLM Stellar Asset Contract id
TIPJAR_CONTRACT_ID=          # C... deployed TipJar contract id

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [CONVEX] Treasury — a project-owned testnet account, PUBLIC KEY ONLY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used read-only: it is the source account for simulating contract reads, which
# need one but never submit anything.
#
# There is deliberately no TREASURY_SECRET. Nothing in this codebase signs as the
# treasury — new wallets are funded through Smart Account Kit — so there is no
# Stellar secret key anywhere in this environment at all.
TREASURY_PUBLIC=             # G... musea-treasury public key
SEED_AMOUNT=100              # test XLM granted to each newly provisioned wallet

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [CONVEX] Passkey smart accounts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The OpenZeppelin smart-account WASM hash and the on-chain verifier that checks
# secp256r1 WebAuthn assertions. Both are published deployments of the Smart
# Account Kit's own contracts — they are not ours and we do not deploy them.
#
# A smart account's ADDRESS is derived from these, so changing either one
# orphans every account already created. Treat them as append-only.
SMART_ACCOUNT_WASM_HASH=     # 64 lowercase hex characters
WEBAUTHN_VERIFIER_ADDRESS=   # C... on-chain secp256r1 verifier

# The WebAuthn Relying Party ID — the domain a passkey is bound to.
#
# DECIDE THIS BEFORE ANYONE REGISTERS. A credential created under one RP ID does
# not resolve under another, so `localhost` and your deployed hostname hold
# permanently separate accounts, and per-branch preview URLs are fundamentally
# incompatible with passkeys.
WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=localhost

# Origins accepted when verifying an assertion. Optional: defaults to
# http://<rp id> for localhost and https://<rp id> otherwise. Set it only for an
# origin that is neither. Comma-separated; the scheme is required.
# WEBAUTHN_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com,https://www.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [CONVEX] Gasless submission — OpenZeppelin Channels
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A contract cannot be a transaction's source or pay its fee, so the relayer
# supplies the source account, sequence number and fee. Get a key at
# https://channels.openzeppelin.com/testnet/gen
#
# THE API KEY MUST NEVER REACH THE CLIENT. It authorises spending someone else's
# XLM on fees: a leaked key is an open relay, not a data leak. This is also why
# there is no Convex httpAction proxy in front of it.
# RELAYER_URL=https://channels.openzeppelin.com/testnet   # optional; this is the default
RELAYER_API_KEY=             # SECRET. Convex env only.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [CONVEX] Auth — passkeys only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Better Auth is used for session management and nothing else. Email and
# password are DISABLED in convex/auth.ts, and no OAuth provider is enabled;
# signing in is a WebAuthn assertion from the same passkey that authorises tips.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=          # openssl rand -base64 32

# Better Auth's base URL and trusted origin. Its host must match WEBAUTHN_RP_ID
# in production — keeping auth same-origin is what stops Safari's ITP from
# dropping the session cookie.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Generated by the Better Auth Convex component on first run, not by hand. The
# private half is a SECRET; the public JWKS is served to verify session tokens.
# SESSION_PRIVATE_JWK=
# SESSION_PUBLIC_JWKS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [CONVEX] Diagnostics
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Attaches the full error — cause chain, stack frames, the fields these errors
# hide outside `message` — to the ConvexError the browser receives, where the
# profile and tip sheet render it in a copyable panel.
#
# Server-side logging is unconditional either way; grep the Convex logs for
# [musea]. KEEP THIS OFF FOR A DEMO.
# DEBUG_ERRORS=false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [CONVEX] Link enrichment — all optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# convex/linkPreview.ts reads oEmbed and Open Graph to turn a pasted URL into a
# card. No AI. YouTube, TikTok, X and Pinterest need no credentials at all.
#
# Instagram is the exception: its oEmbed endpoint requires a Meta app token in
# the form {app-id}|{client-token}. Leave this unset and Instagram links fall
# back to the generic og: scrape rather than failing — which is why it is
# commented out rather than blank.
# INSTAGRAM_OEMBED_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [WEB] Public — safe to expose, these ship to the browser
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Printed by `pnpm --filter @musea/backend dev` on first run.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=              # https://<deployment>.convex.cloud
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_SITE_URL=         # https://<deployment>.convex.site  (.site, not .cloud)
# Optional. The auth client derives its origin from window.location, so previews and
# prod work with this unset. Set it only to pin an absolute origin; a stale value here
# ships into the bundle and breaks sign-in on the deployed site.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_NETWORK=testnet
NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_EXPERT_BASE=https://stellar.expert/explorer/testnet
